;;; special_form_value_refusal_test.esk
;;;
;;; LE-16 negative control: special forms are NOT builtins and the audit in
;;; builtins_first_class_test_*.esk deliberately excludes every name in
;;; tests/coverage/language_surface.json's "special_forms" list from its
;;; iteration. This program pins the OTHER half of that claim: referencing a
;;; special form as a bare value is a documented compile-time refusal, not
;;; silence and not a crash.
;;;
;;; This program is INTENDED to fail to compile, the same shape as
;;; undefined_variable_refusal_test.esk. The parser binds each of these names
;;; to a dedicated AST op (ESHKOL_IF_OP, ESHKOL_DEFINE_OP, ...), so there is
;;; no codegenVariable binding to fall back to and no first-class value could
;;; be synthesized even in principle -- unlike a builtin, which just needs a
;;; row in the lookupInlineBuiltin table (see LE-16 in
;;; .icc/ledger/entries/LE-16.yaml). Every one of these five names is a
;;; documented special form (docs/reference/language special-forms
;;; reference), so this is the expected, LOUD refusal rather than the SIGSEGV
;;; class LE-01 fixed for builtins.
(display (list if define quote lambda set!))
